"Travel Reduction Program | Maricopa County, AZ (https://www.maricopa.gov/2388/Travel-Reduction-Program)\nciteturn962view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.maricopa.gov/2388/Travel-Reduction-Program\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 116\nL0: ###\nL1: \nL2: 【0†Skip to Main Content】\nL3: \nL4: [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL5: \nL6: [Input: Search] [Input]\nL7: \nL8:   1. 【1†Home】\nL9:   2. 【2†Departments】\nL10:   3. 【3†Air Quality】\nL11:   4. Travel Reduction Program\nL12: \nL13: [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL14: # Travel Reduction Program\nL15: \nL16: 【4†Image: Image of Valley Metro Light Rail car】\nL17: The Travel Reduction Program (TRP) began in 1989 as part of the State of Arizona's response to a court ruling requiring greater efforts to 【5†reduce air pollution】. The approximately 80 million commuter miles driven each weekday are a significant contributor to regional air pollution (ozone, particulate matter). One outcome of the ruling was the legislation of TRP 【6†state statutes†www.azleg.gov】 that focus on employers and schools.\nL18: Subsequent revisions to the statute and related Maricopa County ordinance (P-7) reduced the minimum employee site count to 50.\nL19: ## TRP Goals\nL20: Employers and schools are asked to reduce single occupant vehicle (SOV) trips and/or miles traveled to the work site by 10 percent each year for a total of five years, and then five percent for three additional years, or until a 60 percent rate of SOV travel is reached. Progress is tracked through an annual commute survey of employer/school sites.\nL21: The results of the survey are used to develop an annual travel reduction plan that commits the employer/school to implementing and documenting various strategies to reduce SOV trips or miles.\nL22: ## TRP Regional Task Force\nL23: \nL24: The 【7†TRP Regional Task Force】 reviews employer/school survey results and the related plans are officially approved or disapproved. These meetings are open to the public and are usually held every four weeks.\nL25: \nL26: For any organizations seeking to be listed on the Task Force agenda, please submit all requests by the 1st of the month to TRP@maricopa.gov.\nL27: \nL28:   1. 【8†Meeting Agendas】\nL29:   2. 【9†Approved Meeting Minutes】\nL30: \nL31:   1. 【8†Meeting Agendas】\nL32:   * 【10†12/09/2025】\nL33:   * 【11†01/13/2026】\nL34:   * 【12†02/10/2026】\nL35:   * 【13†03/03/2026】\nL36:   * 【14†04/07/2026】\nL37:   * 【15†05/05/2026】\nL38:   * 【16†06/09/2026】\nL39:   * 【17†07/14/2026】\nL40:   * 【18†08/11/2026】\nL41:   * 【19†09/15/2026】\nL42:   * 【20†10/06/2026】\nL43:   * 【21†11/03/2026】\nL44: \nL45:   1. 【9†Approved Meeting Minutes】\nL46: \nL47:   * 【22†12/09/2025】\nL48:   * 【23†01/13/2026】\nL49:   * 【24†02/10/2026】\nL50:   * 【25†03/03/2026】\nL51:   * 【26†04/07/2026】\nL52:   * 【27†05/05/2026】\nL53:   * 【28†06/09/2026】\nL54:   * 【29†07/14/2026】\nL55:   * 【30†08/11/2026】\nL56:   * 【31†09/15/2026】\nL57: ## Contact Us\nL58: \nL59: To contact the Travel Reduction Program, call 602-506-6750 or email TRP@maricopa.gov.\nL60: \nL61: 【32†Image: Best Workplaces for Commuters Badge】\nL62: \nL63: Page reviewed 29 October 2026\nL64: \nL65: 【33†Image†www.facebook.com】\nL66: \nL67:   1. 【34†Image: Maricopa County Seal】\nL68: 301 West Jefferson Street\nL69: Phoenix, Arizona 85003\nL70: Main Line:  602-506-3011\nL71: ### 【35†Using This Site】\nL72: \nL73:   1. 【36†Sitemap】\nL74: \nL75:   2. 【37†Accessibility】\nL76: \nL77:   3. 【38†Copyright Notices】\nL78: \nL79:   4. 【39†Site Terms & Privacy Policy】\nL80: \nL81:   5. 【1†Home】\nL82: \nL83:   *   *   *   *   *   * ### 【40†Residents】\nL84: \nL85:   1. 【41†Contact Us】\nL86: \nL87:   2. 【42†Board Meetings and Agendas】\nL88: \nL89:   3. 【43†Organizational Chart】\nL90: \nL91:   4. 【44†Volunteer/Intern Opportunities】\nL92: \nL93:   5. 【45†Required Postings】\nL94: \nL95:   6. 【46†ADA Compliance】\nL96: ### 【47†V